<title>GERMANY: German state NRW Jan CPI up 0.4 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>German state NRW Jan CPI up 0.4 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The statistics office of the German state of North Rhine-Westphalia reported the following consumer prices changes for January.</p>
<p>    Cost of living		   January	  December</p>
<p>    Mth/mth (pct change)	    +0.4		+0.4</p>
<p>    Year/year			   +2.0		+1.6</p>
<p>Note - These data are later combined with data from three other major German states to calculate the preliminary inflation figure for the whole of west Germany.  </p>
<p>The Statistics Office gave the following breakdown of its cost of living data :</p>
<p>						 Percentage change</p>
<p> Index/component			   mth/mth   yr/yr    Index</p>
<p> Without seasonal goods		  0.3	 2.0	115.4</p>
<p> Without heating oils &amp; Fuels	  0.4	 1.9	114.7</p>
<p> Without rental costs		    0.4	 1.6	112.1</p>
<p> Without service and repair	    0.5	 2.0	113.5</p>
<p> Heating oil, motor fuel only	  1.4	 8.6	121.4</p>
<p> Service and repair only		 0.4	 2.4	119.8</p>
<p> Rents					 0.4	 3.6	126.6</p>
<p> Household energy			  1.8	 5.3	101.2</p>
<p> Personal goods, services and other  1.9	 3.0	112.6</p>
<p> Transport and communications	  0.3	 1.0	114.7</p>
<p> Furniture				   0.2	 1.0	111.5</p>
<p> Foodstuffs, drinks, tobacco	   0.7	 1.4	109.9</p>
<p> Clothing, shoes			   0.1	 1.1	112.5</p>
<p> Health and personal care items	unch	2.1	114.4</p>
<p> Education, entertainment, leisure   1.9	 3.0	112.6</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
